    "   \"id\": \"45579067\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1. Variable Overview & Normality Check\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Understanding the p-value.** Each test below starts from a *null hypothesis* — here that the variable **is normally distributed**. The **p-value** is the probability of seeing data this far from a normal shape purely by chance *if that null hypothesis were true*.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **p > 0.05** → not enough evidence to reject → treat as **Normal**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **p ≤ 0.05** → strong evidence against the null → **Not normal**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"`α = 0.05` is the 5% significance threshold we compare the p-value against.\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"899ad06a43f34b06\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"595ed8c4\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"execution\": {\n",
    "     \"iopub.execute_input\": \"2026-07-22T12:41:41.212026Z\",\n",
    "     \"iopub.status.busy\": \"2026-07-22T12:41:41.211946Z\",\n",
    "     \"iopub.status.idle\": \"2026-07-22T12:41:41.488978Z\",\n",
    "     \"shell.execute_reply\": \"2026-07-22T12:41:41.487804Z\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-07-27T19:45:57.594271Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-07-27T19:45:57.334501Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for ax, col, color in zip(axes, [X_COL, Y_COL], ['steelblue', 'teal']):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    sns.histplot(df[col], kde=True, bins=30, color=color, edgecolor='white', ax=ax)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.axvline(df[col].mean(),   color='crimson',    lw=1.8, linestyle='--', label=f'Mean {df[col].mean():.2f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.axvline(df[col].median(), color='darkorange', lw=1.8, linestyle=':',  label=f'Median {df[col].median():.2f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title(col.replace('_', ' '))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.legend(fontsize=9)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig.suptitle('Distribution of Key Variables', fontsize=13)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Normality tests (D'Agostino-Pearson — works for n > 20)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for col in [X_COL, Y_COL]:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stat, p = stats.normaltest(df[col])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f'{col}: stat={stat:.3f}, p={p:.3e}  → {\\\"Normal\\\" if p > 0.05 else \\\"Not normal\\\"} (α=0.05)')\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"<Figure size 1430x440 with 2 Axes>\"\n",
    "      ],\n",
    "      \"image/png\": \"\"\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"display_data\",\n",
    "     \"jetTransient\": {\n",
    "      \"display_id\": null\n",
    "     }\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"Avg_Daily_Usage_Hours: stat=362.323, p=2.102e-79  → Not normal (α=0.05)\\n\",\n",
    "      \"Mental_Health_Score: stat=462.316, p=4.068e-101  → Not normal (α=0.05)\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 2\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"6e0caa2d\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2. Correlation Analysis\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We report both **Pearson** (linear) and **Spearman** (rank-based, robust to non-normality) correlations.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Understanding the p-value.** For a correlation, the *null hypothesis* is that there is **no relationship** between the two variables (true correlation = 0). The **p-value** is the probability of observing a correlation at least this strong by chance if that null were true.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **p ≤ 0.05** → the correlation is **statistically significant** (unlikely to be a fluke)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **p > 0.05** → not enough evidence that a real relationship exists\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"1924825c54792830\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"673e3384\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"execution\": {\n",
    "     \"iopub.execute_input\": \"2026-07-22T12:41:41.493845Z\",\n",
    "     \"iopub.status.busy\": \"2026-07-22T12:41:41.493610Z\",\n",
    "     \"iopub.status.idle\": \"2026-07-22T12:41:41.503397Z\",\n",
    "     \"shell.execute_reply\": \"2026-07-22T12:41:41.502775Z\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-07-27T19:45:57.680238Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-07-27T19:45:57.662310Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"pearson_r,  pearson_p  = stats.pearsonr( df[X_COL], df[Y_COL])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"spearman_r, spearman_p = stats.spearmanr(df[X_COL], df[Y_COL])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def interpret_r(r):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    a = abs(r)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if a < 0.1:  return 'negligible'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if a < 0.3:  return 'weak'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if a < 0.5:  return 'moderate'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if a < 0.7:  return 'strong'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return 'very strong'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"results = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'Method':    ['Pearson', 'Spearman'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'r':         [round(pearson_r,  4), round(spearman_r,  4)],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'p-value':   [pearson_p,            spearman_p],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'Significant (α=0.05)': [pearson_p < 0.05, spearman_p < 0.05],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    'Interpretation': [interpret_r(pearson_r), interpret_r(spearman_r)],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(results.to_string(index=False))\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"  Method       r  p-value  Significant (α=0.05) Interpretation\\n\",\n",
    "      \" Pearson -0.8165      0.0                  True    very strong\\n\",\n",
    "      \"Spearman -0.8401      0.0                  True    very strong\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 3\n",
    "  },\n",
